# Two tables every change appends a row to. Two branches that each add a row conflict on
# the same line for no reason: both rows are wanted. With the union merge, git keeps both
# when it merges locally. Check the result when two branches edited the same existing row:
# both versions are kept, and one has to be removed by hand.
docs/open-questions.md merge=union
docs/09-plan/progress.md merge=union
